  lean-qit-qlg/QIT/LICENSE).

lean-qit-qlg/QAlg/
  Source statements from https://github.com/QudeLeap/Lean-QuantumAlg-Bench
  (Apache License, Version 2.0, Copyright 2026 QudeLeap; see
  lean-qit-qlg/QAlg/LICENSE).


Libraries and tools
-------------------

chemlib/ and the Lake projects under icho2026/
  Apache License, Version 2.0, Copyright 2026 FrenzyMath (see the LICENSE
  file in each directory). AFPS2017 formalizes claims from Mijalis et al.
  (2017), "A fully automated flow-based approach for accelerated peptide
  synthesis", Nature Chemical Biology 13, 464-466.

imo2026/tools/lean4export/
  A copy of https://github.com/leanprover/lean4export (Apache License,
  Version 2.0; see imo2026/tools/lean4export/LICENSE).

putnambench/humanize/
  A snapshot of https://github.com/PolyArch/humanize, vendored unchanged so the
  PutnamBench run can be reproduced exactly. It is distributed under that
  project's terms.

Lean dependencies
  The Lake projects fetch, but do not include, Lean 4
  (https://github.com/leanprover/lean4), Mathlib
  (https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4), Physlib
  (https://github.com/leanprover-community/physlib), PhysLean
  (https://github.com/HEPLean/PhysLean), CSLib
  (https://github.com/leanprover/cslib), Comparator
  (https://github.com/leanprover/comparator) and Landrun
  (https://github.com/Zouuup/landrun). Each is under its own license.
